{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "readme": [
    "SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for model rates. Consumed at BUILD TIME by both engines:",
    "  Rust: src-tauri/src/commands/pricing.rs  (include_str! + serde)",
    "  TS:   src/lib/modelPricing.ts            (JSON import)",
    "There is no second table. Do not add rate literals to either language.",
    "",
    "Matching: entries are evaluated IN ARRAY ORDER, first match wins. Both engines",
    "build the same candidate list for a model id (lowercased+trimmed, then with a",
    "known route prefix stripped, then with a trailing -YYYYMMDD date stripped) and",
    "test each candidate against `equals` / `prefix` / `contains`. List specific",
    "rows ABOVE generic ones.",
    "",
    "Rates are USD per 1M tokens. `cacheRead` / `cacheWrite5m` / `cacheWrite1h` are",
    "absolute rates, not multipliers, so a vendor changing its multiplier cannot",
    "silently rewrite every row.",
    "",
    "`schedule` replaces `rates` when a published rate changes on a known date.",
    "Entries are evaluated against the date OF THE PRICED TURN (not today), so a",
    "turn billed in August stays billed at August's rate forever.",
    "",
    "`inputIncludesCacheRead` records the vendor's token semantics: true when the",
    "reported input/prompt token count is a SUPERSET that already contains the",
    "cached-read tokens (OpenAI `cached_tokens`), false when the buckets are",
    "disjoint (Anthropic `input_tokens` excludes cache_read/cache_creation). The",
    "shared cost primitive in both engines is purely additive over disjoint",
    "buckets; callers holding superset payloads must normalise before calling.",
    "See CE1 in dev/cost-efficiency-loop.md."
  ],
